<?php $groups=[];foreach($student['rows'] as $r){$groups[(int)$r['semester']][]=$r;}foreach($groups as $sem=>$modules):$total=0;$weight=$weights[(int)ceil($sem/2)-1]/2;foreach($modules as $i=>$r):$total+=(float)$r['mark']*(float)$r['credits'];?><tr><?php if($i===0):?><td rowspan="<?=count($modules)+2?>"><?=$roman[$sem]?></td><?php endif;?><td><?=e($r['module_code'])?></td><td class="module-title"><?=e($r['module_title'])?></td><td><?=$r['passing_year']?></td><td><?=rtrim(rtrim(number_format((float)$r['maximum'],2,'.',''),'0'),'.')?></td><td><?=number_format((float)$r['mark'],2)?></td><td><?=rtrim(rtrim(number_format((float)$r['credits'],2,'.',''),'0'),'.')?></td><td><?=number_format((float)$r['mark']*(float)$r['credits'],2)?></td></tr><?php endforeach;?><tr class="semester-total"><td colspan="6">Total</td><td><?=number_format($total,2)?></td></tr><tr class="semester-weight"><td colspan="3">Weighting Carried Over</td><td colspan="3"><?=$weight?>% of the total</td><td><b><?=number_format($total*$weight/100,2)?></b></td></tr><?php endforeach;?></tbody></table>
<div class="result-summary"><div>Maximum Credits Carried Over: <b><?=number_format($student['denominator']/2,2)?></b><br>Total Credit Secured: <b><?=number_format($student['numerator']/2,2)?></b></div><div>Percentage secured: <b><?=number_format($student['percent'],2)?>%</b><br>Level of performance: <b><?=e($student['performance'])?></b></div></div><div class="issued">Issued on: <b><?=e(date('F j, Y',strtotime($c['issued_on'])))?></b></div><footer class="signatures"><div><div class="signature-space"></div><b><?=e($settings['dean'])?></b><br>Dean of Academic Affairs</div><div class="seal-space">College Seal</div><div><div class="signature-space"></div><b><?=e($settings['president'])?></b><br>President</div></footer></article>
<article class="result-page back" data-student="<?=e((string)$sid)?>"><h2>Level of Performance</h2><p>Assessment is primarily a matter of academic judgement, and the computational structure is designed to facilitate consistent judgements. The following scale is used as a way of relating judgement of performance to a numerical mark.</p><table class="performance"><thead><tr><th>Judgement of Performance</th><th>Mark</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Outstanding</td><td>80% and above</td></tr><tr><td>Very Good</td><td>70% - 79.9%</td></tr><tr><td>Good</td><td>60% - 69.9%</td></tr><tr><td>Satisfactory</td><td>50% - 59.9%</td></tr><tr><td>Fail</td><td>49.9% and below</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="weighting-intro">The overall mark for a student at the end of a programme reflects his or her entire performance throughout the period of study. The final mark is a combination of the overall mark of all the years weighted in the following manner:</p><div class="programme-weights"><p><span>2-year programme</span>30: 70 (year I: year II)</p><p><span>3-year programme</span>20: 30: 50 (year I: year II: year III)</p><p><span>4-year programme</span>10: 20: 30: 40 (year I: year II: year III: year IV)</p></div></article><?php endforeach;?></body></html>
